<title>USA: Clayton Homes says tops $1 bln annual revs.</title>
<headline>Clayton Homes says tops $1 bln annual revs.</headline>
<dateline>KNOXVILLE, Tenn. 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Clayton Homes Inc said Monday that it exceeded $1 billion in revenues for the fiscal year ended June 30, a strategic objective it set five years ago.</p>
<p>&quot;This is an important chapter in the company's book of accomplishments,&quot; said Jim Clayton, Clayton founder, chairman and chief executive officer.  &quot;We look to double the business again by the year 2002.&quot;</p>
<p>Clayton is a vertically integrated company in the manufactured housing industry, operates 67 manufactured-home communities and provides a variety of financial services to home buyers.</p>
</text>
